<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-chapter-Common-Discrete-RVs" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Common Discrete Random Variables</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> The problem sets provided here will give you more practice with discrete random variables. The first six sections each focus on a different common discrete random variable. The final section will challenge your ability to identify which random variables are appropriate in various scenarios.  </p>

      <p> Each problem set contains two types of problems: interactive exercises and non-interactive ("written") exercises. You will be able to check your answers and get immediate feedback on the interactive portion.
      </p>

      <p> Note: This is a work in progress. These problems sets for 5.2-5.7  are still being edited and solutions checked for accuracy and clarity.
      </p>
  </introduction>

